 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? French intermediate really is the golden year of languages, where you have enough to say without it feeling like school. Have you tried speaking it with native speakers, even if it' just a little? It is, and it gets easier. You could also try shadowing with cartoons, there's lot of French content online. It is, but little bit every day adds up. Another technique is talking to yourself, as silly as it looks. Your brain doesn't care, it thinks you' actually having a conversation. That' a great idea, and you can listen to yourself in years to come and see how far you' come.",
